--- !u!114 &-3124322356879708659
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "As you\u2019ve heard a few times up to this point, when you\u2019re in Play mode, none of the changes you make are saved. Make sure to pay attention when entering and exiting Play mode so that you don't lose your changes! \n\nBy default, the <b>Editor</b> windows around the <b>Game</b> view become a tiny bit darker when you enter Play mode to help visually distinguish between Play mode and Edit mode \u2014 this is known as the <b>Play mode tint.</b> \n\nIn this step, you\u2019ll edit the <b>Play</b> mode tint to make it more noticeable so that you\u2019ll always realize when you\u2019re in Play mode and avoid losing unsaved changes."
--- !u!114 &-2952087227044479996
